HADOOP WORDCOUNT PROGRAM – COMMANDS AND OUTPUT

1. Format Hadoop Namenode:

~/hadoop/bin/hdfs namenode -format

2. Check Hadoop Version:

~/hadoop/bin/hadoop version

3. Start HDFS:

~/hadoop/sbin/start-dfs.sh

4. Start YARN:

~/hadoop/sbin/start-yarn.sh

5. Check Running Hadoop Services:

jps

Expected Output:

NameNode
DataNode
SecondaryNameNode
ResourceManager
NodeManager
Jps

6. Create WordCount Directory:

mkdir -p ~/wordcount

7. Create Input File:

echo "hello hadoop hello world hadoop big data hello" > ~/wordcount/input.txt

8. Create HDFS Input Directory:

~/hadoop/bin/hdfs dfs -mkdir -p /input

9. Upload Input File to HDFS:

~/hadoop/bin/hdfs dfs -put ~/wordcount/input.txt /input/

10. Execute WordCount Program:

~/hadoop/bin/hadoop jar ~/hadoop-2.7.3/share/hadoop/mapreduce/hadoop-mapreduce-examples-2.7.3.jar wordcount /input /output

11. Display WordCount Output:

~/hadoop/bin/hdfs dfs -cat /output/part-r-00000

OUTPUT:

big     1
data    1
hadoop  2
hello   3
world   1

12. View Original Input File:

cd ~/wordcount

cat input.txt

INPUT:

hello hadoop hello world hadoop big data hello

